<h1><span lang="EN-US">Deactivate</span></h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from the</span> <b><i style="font-weight:normal; font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>tree context menu</b></span> <span class="Path">for</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Transformation &gt; Deactivate</b></span></i></b><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">Description:</span></b> <span lang="EN-GB">This command cancels the scanning and capturing through active transformation.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: To use this command scanning should be enabled in your dongle options.</p>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use Deactivate</b></span><span lang="EN-US">:</span></p>
<p class="whs4"><span lang="EN-US">1.When you don’t want to scan through an active transformation or</span></p>
<p class="whs4"><span lang="EN-US">2.When creating new transformation with option Capture switched on.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Related topic:</b></span> &#160;<a href="activate_for_scanning.htm">Activate for Scanning</a></p>
